-[all chuckle]

17:15.667 --> 17:17.292
No, I'm… I'm just joking around.

17:17.833 --> 17:20.417
This is gonna free up more of my time
as we focus on scaling up.

17:20.500 --> 17:22.833
So, does anyone have anything for Cardify?

17:26.125 --> 17:27.125
Anyone?

17:29.042 --> 17:31.917
-And how about Tinder?
-[clamoring]

17:32.000 --> 17:34.417
I got a little something.
Excuse me, folks. Sorry.

17:34.500 --> 17:35.875
What's… What's happening? I don't…

17:35.958 --> 17:37.583
Fellas, coming through. Excuse me, sorry.

17:38.625 --> 17:41.458
So, I'm getting out of the shower.

17:41.542 --> 17:42.917
-[Diego] Ooh, sexy.
-[all chuckling]

17:43.000 --> 17:45.250
And, for context, I like my showers hot.

17:45.750 --> 17:47.542
'Kay, the whole bathroom
fills up with steam, so,

17:47.625 --> 17:50.667
I go to wipe off the mirror,
and what do I see?

17:51.667 --> 17:53.458
I see this beautiful face
staring right back at me.

17:53.542 --> 17:55.417
I thought to myself,
"Okay, this is fun." [chuckles]

17:55.500 --> 17:58.375
So, so, so I let the mirror
fog up again, right?

17:58.458 --> 18:00.250
I wipe it away again,
this time to the left.

18:00.333 --> 18:02.250
And now I'm thinking to myself,
"Okay, this is…

18:02.333 --> 18:04.167
-this is really fun."
-This is why he's always late?

18:04.250 --> 18:05.708
-[all chuckling]
-Look… look,

18:05.792 --> 18:07.375
in the app, we're using buttons right now

18:07.458 --> 18:09.167
to say "yes" or "no"
to somebody's dating profile,

18:09.250 --> 18:12.500
but it is clunky. It is sluggish.

18:12.583 --> 18:13.583
However,

18:14.250 --> 18:16.583
swiping in one direction
if you like the person's profile,

18:16.667 --> 18:19.708
swiping in the opposite direction
if you don't like the profile,

18:19.792 --> 18:23.542
it makes it all one…
one smooth, fluid motion.

18:23.625 --> 18:25.542
It's organic.
It's how the mind already works,

18:25.625 --> 18:27.000
and it's fun.

18:27.542 --> 18:29.708
-Mmm. What do you guys think?
-[employees murmuring]

18:31.292 --> 18:33.167
-Yeah, I kinda like that.
-Yeah, no, actually I think what

18:33.250 --> 18:35.333
-this does best is differentiate us from--
-Y'know, I like the swipe.

18:35.417 --> 18:36.958
The swipe is cool. But, uh,

18:37.042 --> 18:39.792
we won't have time to program it
before my campus marketing push.

18:39.875 --> 18:42.833
Well, this would be a good time to say
that Tisha and I have actually

18:42.917 --> 18:44.042
been programming it for the last week,

18:44.125 --> 18:46.958
-and it is already in the new update.
-I'll need to be briefed on that first.

18:47.042 --> 18:48.292
-Right, Sean?
-[Sean] But does it work?

18:48.375 --> 18:49.417
See for yourself.

18:53.667 --> 18:56.708
Okay, everybody, uh, check your phones

18:57.375 --> 18:59.417
because right now, ladies and gentlemen,

18:59.500 --> 19:00.500
the swipe

19:01.292 --> 19:02.417
is live.

19:05.958 --> 19:08.417
-Uh, it says I need to update.
-Yeah, you gotta do the update

19:08.500 --> 19:09.500
first, obviously.

19:10.500 --> 19:12.375
-If you just… That one there.
-[Sean] Okay, yeah.

19:12.458 --> 19:14.042
-It's just installing. Do you have it yet?
-Mmm.

19:14.583 --> 19:16.250
It's still… still cooking.

19:16.333 --> 19:17.958
-[Sean] Give it a second.
-[phone chiming]

19:18.042 --> 19:20.708
-All right, all right, I got it. Um…
-[employee 3] Oh, you got it?

19:21.208 --> 19:22.583
Oh, yeah, this is pretty slick.

19:22.667 --> 19:24.292
-[employees] Look, yeah, check it out.
-[Sean] Okay.

19:24.375 --> 19:26.750
-[employee 1] Dude, this is impressive.
-[Tisha] Okay, so…

19:26.833 --> 19:28.042
-Oh!
-You sign in?

19:28.125 --> 19:30.375
-[employee] That's me. Look at that.
-[employee 2] Good picture, man.

19:30.458 --> 19:33.083
-[employee 3] It's intuitive.
-[employee 4] I'm beginning to like it.

19:33.167 --> 19:35.083
-Oh. [chuckles]
-I'll swipe on you.

19:35.167 --> 19:37.250
Yeah, it's like dealing cards.
Hell yeah, JB.

19:37.333 --> 19:38.458
[chuckles] Thanks. And Tisha.

19:38.542 --> 19:40.125
Can we load up some more starter accounts?

19:40.208 --> 19:41.917
So that they're not,
like, staring at blank screens?

19:42.000 --> 19:43.458
I think we should
go with this version tomorrow.

19:43.542 --> 19:45.583
-Definitely. E-mail Brent right now.
-[Sean] Yeah, thank you.

19:45.667 --> 19:46.958
Guys, this is how you gamify.

19:47.833 --> 19:50.250
Mmm, yeah, but her face is kinda beat.

19:50.333 --> 19:52.250
-When has that ever stopped you?
-Bro, shut up.

19:52.333 --> 19:53.333
You know what I'm talking about.

19:53.417 --> 19:55.833
-The redhead is way, way hotter.
-No. No, she's dressed like a pirate's--

19:55.917 --> 19:58.125
-Oh, yo, uh, we're doing the…
-Hey.

19:58.208 --> 19:59.417
Getting some photos

19:59.500 --> 20:01.000
-selected for the demo.
-Pictures for the demo.

20:01.083 --> 20:02.083
-Yeah.
-Yeah?

20:02.167 --> 20:03.458
-Mmm.
-Okay, let me see.

20:07.542 --> 20:09.083
[chuckles] Yep.

20:10.292 --> 20:11.292
Okay.

20:12.125 --> 20:13.125
No, not… not her.

20:13.208 --> 20:14.583
-Yes! Do the redhead.
-[Justin] Mmm. [scoffs]

20:14.667 --> 20:15.875
Whew, she's super hot.

20:16.375 --> 20:18.375
Whitney, you dog. Thank you.

20:18.458 --> 20:19.708
-What'd I say?
-[chuckles]

20:19.792 --> 20:21.042
You wanted to see me?

20:21.125 --> 20:22.792
Yes, yes, I did.

20:23.292 --> 20:25.833
Um, care to talk over a game?

20:26.875 --> 20:28.125
-Ping-Pong?
-Yeah, Ping-Pong.

20:28.708 --> 20:29.708
I could try.

20:31.458 --> 20:32.833
-Yep!
-[grunting] Oh!

20:36.000 --> 20:38.125
-[grunts, exclaims]
-Fuck!

20:38.208 --> 20:40.958
-[laughs]
-Oh, my God. [groans]

20:41.042 --> 20:42.333
-I got it, I got it.
-Come on. Go again.

20:42.417 --> 20:43.708
-[Whitney] Ready?
-Come on, come on.

20:46.458 --> 20:48.208
-You're actually really good at this.
-Yeah,

20:48.292 --> 20:50.958
I grew up with a Ping-Pong table
in our rec room, so…

20:51.042 --> 20:53.875
-Yo! No! No! [chuckles]
-Yes! That's right. Oh, yes!

20:53.958 --> 20:56.292
[exclaims] Okay, go ahead. Sorry.

20:56.375 --> 20:58.208
-Wait, uh, what's the score?
-[groans]

20:58.292 --> 21:00.292
Uh, 17 you, 14 me. Whoa.

21:00.375 --> 21:02.417
-Whoa. You knew I wasn't ready. [chuckles]
-[exclaims]

21:02.500 --> 21:05.917
That's incredibly unsportsmanlike.
You're gonna have to make it up to me.

21:06.000 --> 21:07.833
-Uh, how about a work dinner?
-[chuckling]

21:07.917 --> 21:10.208
Tomorrow night.
Catch me up on your marketing plan.

21:10.292 --> 21:12.917
No, I can't.
I-I leave for SMU in the morning.

21:13.000 --> 21:14.958
Well, then come tonight.

21:15.042 --> 21:16.250
It's my uncle's birthday dinner.

21:16.333 --> 21:18.917
My mom always makes
way too much food anyway.

21:19.000 --> 21:20.458
Oh, what, at your family's house?

21:20.958 --> 21:22.583
-Uh, I don't wanna in--
-No, no, no. [stammering]

21:22.667 --> 21:25.625
They'll love you. They liked Diego, and
he's like the worst person I've ever met.

21:26.125 --> 21:27.583
-Fuck you, bitch.
-Oh, he heard me.

21:28.417 --> 21:29.417
-Whoa.
-Hey, Diego,

21:29.500 --> 21:31.708
my cousin has a boyfriend now,
so don't do the thing--

21:31.792 --> 21:34.458
-Bro, I know. I'm just here for the food.
-Okay.

21:34.542 --> 21:37.083
-[partygoers chattering]
-[Justin] Hey, what's up, buddy?

21:37.583 --> 21:39.500
Britney, how you been?

21:39.583 --> 21:40.958
-Come on, man.
-[child] Justin!

21:41.042 --> 21:43.542
-[chuckling] Hey, what's going on, buddy?
-Whoa! [chuckles]

21:43.625 --> 21:46.083
-Justin. Hi, sweetie.
-Hi, Aunt Gayle. Hi, hi.

21:46.167 --> 21:47.458
-This is Whitney.
-Oh.

21:47.542 --> 21:48.833
-Hi, how are you?
-Hi. I'm Whitney.

21:48.917 --> 21:50.708
Oh, Whitney, this is Ella.

21:50.792 --> 21:53.542
-[gasps] Oh, hi, Ella.
-Aw.

21:53.625 --> 21:56.083
-Oh, she smiled. Oh, my God.
-Hey, what's going on?

21:56.167 --> 21:57.167
-Hi.
-Good to see you.

21:57.250 --> 21:58.292
-Hi.
-[Justin] Good to see you.

21:58.375 --> 21:59.625
-What's going on?
-[partygoer] Justin!

21:59.708 --> 22:02.083
-Hey! What's happening?
-[partygoer] There he is!

22:03.000 --> 22:04.542
-[Whitney] Sorry!
-What's the matter with you?

22:04.625 --> 22:06.583
Showing up two hours late. Dinner's over.

22:06.667 --> 22:07.875
-I showed up.
-[groans]

22:07.958 --> 22:10.208
-Hi. Mom, this Whitney from work.
-Look at you.

22:10.292 --> 22:11.458
-Oh. You're adorable.
-Hi.

22:11.542 --> 22:13.250
-Sit down. Please, make her a plate.
-[Whitney] Oh.

22:13.333 --> 22:15.042
-[Justin's mom] Plenty of leftovers.
-Okay. [chuckles]

22:15.833 --> 22:18.083
So you work with my Justin?

22:18.167 --> 22:19.375
Yes, ma'am.

22:19.458 --> 22:21.292
Been there about, uh, six months.

22:21.375 --> 22:23.417
I don't think it's right
to meet people on the Internet.

22:23.500 --> 22:26.958
I think if you're a good man,
you have no trouble meeting a nice girl.

22:27.042 --> 22:28.250
My Justin's a good man.

22:28.333 --> 22:29.458
-[Justin] Oh.
-Aw. [chuckles]

22:29.542 --> 22:31.208
-I raised you right.
-Mom!

22:31.292 --> 22:32.708
Well, thank you for having me.

22:32.792 --> 22:34.625
Your family is so warm.

22:34.708 --> 22:35.708
-[glass shattering]
-Oh.

22:35.792 --> 22:37.708
-[sighing] Oh, God. Excuse me.
-Oh, God.

22:37.792 --> 22:39.125
-Can I help?
-No, eat.

22:39.208 --> 22:41.792
-Thank you.
-All right, nobody touch anything.

22:41.875 --> 22:43.833
-[Whitney laughing] What's going on?
-Uh, it's chaos. Do you…

22:43.917 --> 22:46.042
-Do you eat everything? Yes?
-Oh, wow. Yes, please.

22:46.125 --> 22:47.667
-Wine? Okay, um.
-Yes.

22:47.750 --> 22:50.208
Pitch me on this dating app idea.

22:50.292 --> 22:52.792
Sean says you're obsessed.
What's going on?

22:53.292 --> 22:56.167
Okay. Um. My first revelation, uh…

22:56.250 --> 22:58.167
Oh, I can help. [chuckles]

22:58.250 --> 23:00.333
Nobody wants to do paperwork.

23:00.417 --> 23:01.750
-[Justin] Right.
-Seriously,

23:01.833 --> 23:05.167
it's, like, make the sign-up process
under two minutes max.

23:05.250 --> 23:07.583
So next is demographics.

23:07.667 --> 23:10.042
You look at your Match.coms,
your e-Harmonys…

23:10.125 --> 23:11.917
-Uh-huh.
-…and it just… it becomes clear

23:12.000 --> 23:14.917
really quickly that young people
are just not using these sites.

23:15.000 --> 23:16.542
-Yeah, they're not cool.
-Right.

23:16.625 --> 23:21.208
It's like you're ad-admitting failure
or social ineptitude

23:21.292 --> 23:23.667
if you have to rely on
a dating site in your 20s.

23:23.750 --> 23:25.292
Wow, that looks good. [chuckles]

23:25.375 --> 23:26.458
I mean, on the other platforms,

23:26.542 --> 23:30.042
I have to really dig
to find any decent guys under 40.

23:30.125 --> 23:32.167
Mmm. So you use the other sites?

23:32.250 --> 23:33.833
Yeah, f… for research.

23:33.917 --> 23:36.500
-Oh, for research. Of course. Of course.
-[chuckles]

23:36.583 --> 23:37.917
And the other thing, right,

23:38.000 --> 23:40.000
-is that they're all websites.
-[Justin] Yeah.

23:40.083 --> 23:41.125
So Hatch's future…

23:41.208 --> 23:43.333
well, the future of everything,
it's just… it's apps.

23:43.417 --> 23:45.833
-Mm-hmm.
-But, at the moment,

23:45.917 --> 23:49.708
we're in the unfortunate position
of trying to launch a dating app

23:49.792 --> 23:53.667
when young people don't date online,
and old people don't do apps.

23:53.750 --> 23:55.708
Okay, you're making me a little nervous.

23:55.792 --> 23:57.500
Am I jumping on a sinking ship?

23:57.583 --> 23:58.708
-No. No.
-What's going on?

23:58.792 --> 24:01.000
I look at this data,
and all I see is potential.

24:01.083 --> 24:02.083
-Okay.
-You know,

24:02.167 --> 24:03.958
if we can just break through that stigma,

24:04.042 --> 24:07.167
suddenly we've got complete market share
of all millennial dating…

24:07.250 --> 24:08.750
-Wow, thank you.
-Mm-hmm.

24:08.833 --> 24:11.833
-The demo that does most of the dating.
-Mm-hmm.

24:11.917 --> 24:15.708
You know, all we need is just one…
[chuckles] …youthful epicenter

24:15.792 --> 24:18.042
to adopt the app, and I just… I…

24:18.125 --> 24:20.417
-I really think it'll catch like wildfire.
-Mmm.

24:20.500 --> 24:21.792
Which is why I said to Sean, you know,

24:21.875 --> 24:24.875
"Just give me 600 bucks and a plane ticket
and I will come back

24:24.958 --> 24:27.458
-with the next Fortune 500 company."
-That is sick.

24:27.542 --> 24:29.417
-Justin.
-Hey-- [groaning]

24:29.500 --> 24:31.833
-[child laughs]
-[laughs]

24:31.917 --> 24:34.042
-Buddy! Oh, my…
-[laughing]

24:34.125 --> 24:36.375
-What did you do?
-I don't know.

24:36.458 --> 24:40.000
[stammers] Why SMU?
Why is Dallas our-our youthful epicenter?

24:40.083 --> 24:42.875
-Please, walk me through that. Keep going.
-[laughs] Okay. Well, I went there…

24:42.958 --> 24:44.292
Go Mustangs.

24:44.375 --> 24:47.458
So, I know the lay of the land
and the Greek life.

24:47.542 --> 24:49.708
-Okay. Just 'cause…
-Hey, honey.

24:49.792 --> 24:50.958
-Mmm.
-Hey.

24:51.042 --> 24:55.167
You don't have some college sweetheart
waiting for you, huh?

24:55.250 --> 24:57.583
No. No, God no.

24:58.750 --> 25:00.500
Why-Why-Why "God no"? What does that mean?

25:01.375 --> 25:03.542
Uh… [sighs] I just had a really…

25:03.625 --> 25:06.250
-a toxic boyfriend back in high school.
-Hmm.

25:06.333 --> 25:08.625
It's actually, like,
not much better in… [laughing] …college.

25:10.292 --> 25:11.458
Guys suck.

25:12.917 --> 25:14.500
Yeah, thanks. [chuckles]

25:14.583 --> 25:16.625
So, like… [stammers] Are you, uh…

25:16.708 --> 25:19.750
Currently you don't… you don't have…

25:19.833 --> 25:20.833
-Right now?
-Yeah.

25:20.917 --> 25:22.875
-No. [chuckles]
-Oh, okay. Okay. That's… No, that's good.

25:22.958 --> 25:24.792
For the best. Don't wanna have
some jealous guy fighting me

25:24.875 --> 25:25.875
when I take you home tonight.

25:28.167 --> 25:30.083
When I drive you home tonight.
When I drive you home.

25:30.667 --> 25:32.833
-Like, after this. Like, not…
-[snickers]

25:32.917 --> 25:34.875
-[laughing] Oh, my God.
-I'm freaking…

25:34.958 --> 25:36.958
[♪ "Bulletproof" plays]

25:42.167 --> 25:45.500
[pants] I graduated not even a year ago.

25:45.583 --> 25:48.042
Why do I feel 40 years older
than these… [chuckling] …girls?

25:48.125 --> 25:50.250
I mean, these girls
scare the fuck out of me,

25:50.333 --> 25:52.958
but you are, like, one of them.
They're gonna love it.

25:56.125 --> 25:57.125
I don't get it.

25:58.292 --> 26:03.208
[stammers] We throw, like, mixers,
parties, uh, cookouts, and formals.

26:03.292 --> 26:07.042
[stammers] Meeting guys is,
like, what we do here.

26:07.125 --> 26:09.458
Yes. No, I get that, uh, totally.

26:09.542 --> 26:11.125
Um, okay.

26:11.208 --> 26:12.458
[exhales sharply]

26:12.542 --> 26:16.208
Have you ever been in a party
and there is this cute guy,

26:16.875 --> 26:19.208
and you're thinking about approaching him,

26:19.292 --> 26:22.667
but you don't [chuckles] 'cause
you're nervous he won't be interested?

26:22.750 --> 26:24.583
Actually, no. Don't answer that.

26:24.667 --> 26:25.917
[chuckling] You are like
the most gorgeous person

26:26.000 --> 26:27.625
-I have ever seen in my life.
-[Kappas chuckle]

26:27.708 --> 26:31.917
But for the rest of us, you know,
how many of you can relate to that?

26:36.125 --> 26:37.917
Kinda? Yes, okay, great.

26:38.000 --> 26:41.542
With Tinder, you're always
starting a conversation with someone

26:41.625 --> 26:43.250
who you already know is interested.

26:44.000 --> 26:45.000
You know what? Let's just, uh,

26:45.083 --> 26:46.375
let's see who's on here. Okay.

26:47.292 --> 26:48.417
So, here we go.

26:48.500 --> 26:51.125
Okay. All right.

26:51.208 --> 26:53.500
Now this is what I'm talking about.

26:53.583 --> 26:54.750
He's a good-looking guy.

26:55.583 --> 26:58.208
Okay, let's keep look… Ugh. No. Mm-mmm.

26:58.292 --> 27:00.125
But look, he's Gryffindor, I'm Ravenclaw.

27:00.208 --> 27:01.500
[scoffs] That is just not meant to be.

27:01.583 --> 27:05.708
That's a no, so I am swiping left. Nope.

27:05.792 --> 27:07.375
Okay. Ooh, Kyle.

27:07.458 --> 27:08.958
Do we like Kyle?

27:09.042 --> 27:11.292
Hmm. You know. Kinda cute.

27:11.375 --> 27:13.000
Uh, oh, wait.

27:13.083 --> 27:15.958
I'm pretty sure
he dated my friend forever ago.

27:16.042 --> 27:19.167
-Pfft. And Kappas don't date Kappas' exes.
-[murmuring] Mm-mmm.

27:19.250 --> 27:22.333
Good. That's a no, so swipe left.

27:23.500 --> 27:24.708
Next.

27:24.792 --> 27:27.208
Huh. This I could get into.

27:27.292 --> 27:31.583
He has, you know,
nice eyes, decent dresser.

27:31.667 --> 27:33.250
I'm swiping right.

27:36.042 --> 27:38.500
Oh! And look at that, we matched.

27:38.583 --> 27:42.792
Okay, so that, that basically means
that we both swiped right on each other.

27:44.417 --> 27:46.250
And he's already sent a message.

27:46.333 --> 27:49.542
